30,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The variance is brutal. February was nearly triple August. We need a system that absorbs that shock.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,The template is a nightmare. It takes hours to key in. I refuse to do that monthly.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The monitors show one room uses four times the energy of another. The payment log shows late payments when bills spike.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The electrician quote is 34,000 yen per room. That is a huge upfront cost. I am hesitant to commit to that.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,I saw the cooler notice. People stopped using it to avoid arguments. That is exactly what I fear.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Jonathan, the disparity is real. If we split equally, the heavy users subsidize the light ones.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Benjamin, but if we split by usage, the admin time kills us. The template proved that.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"We need a middle ground. Maybe a base fee plus a usage meter? It requires some admin, but less than full reconciliation.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"A base fee helps with predictability. But 34,000 yen upfront is a barrier. Can we phase it in?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,I worry that meters make us watch each other. The cooler notice showed how much we avoid each other over small things.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Victoria, phasing it in makes sense. We can start with a base fee and add meters later if needed.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,I like the base fee idea. It’s simple. I can handle a simple calculation. I cannot handle a spreadsheet.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"A base fee covers the fixed costs. Meters cover the variable. It is fair, but it requires trust in the data.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,I can live with a base fee if it is set based on the average of the last year. It gives me stability.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,"If the base fee is fair, maybe we don’t need to watch the meters so closely. We can just trust the average.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Let’s propose three options. One: equal split. Two: base fee plus metered usage. Three: base fee only, adjusted annually.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,I vote for the one that takes the least time. I am tired of being the one who checks the math.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will support the option that ties payment to usage. It eliminates the resentment I see building.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I will support the option that minimizes upfront cost and maximizes predictability. The base fee only option looks promising.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,I will support the option that makes it easiest to talk to each other. I hope we can agree on something kind.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
