59,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option B feels right. It gives us predictability without the guilt of watching a meter tick up every hour.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A is the easiest for me. I just divide by five. No spreadsheets, no meters, no drama.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option C is the most fair. It ensures that the person who uses the most pays the most. It is objective.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Option B is the only one that protects my budget. I can plan for a fixed amount. Option C has too much upfront cost.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option A feels the most peaceful. It doesn’t require us to measure each other. It just asks us to share.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Mio, Option A ignores the winter spike. In February, the light users are subsidizing the heavy users significantly.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"Benjamin, but who wants to argue about that? I want to pay my share and forget about it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,Benjamin is right. The data shows a four-fold difference. Option A is not fair to those who conserve.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"Jonathan, fairness is important, but so is stability. Option B gives me a fixed number. I can save for it.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,I hear you. But I worry that Option C makes us feel like we are being watched. The cooler notice showed how much that hurts.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Victoria, Option B’s annual settlement is a risk. If the year is cold, the final bill could be huge.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,I don’t care about the risk. I care about the time. Option A takes five minutes. Option B takes hours to reconcile.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"The risk is real, but the fairness of Option C is undeniable. We can mitigate the admin burden with a simple app.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I can accept a small annual adjustment. But I cannot accept a 34,000 yen upfront cost. Option C is out for me.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I think Option B is a good compromise. It is predictable, and it doesn’t require us to install meters in our rooms.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I will vote for Option B. It balances predictability with a degree of fairness. It allows us to breathe.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,I will vote for Option A. It is the only one that doesn’t turn my evenings into a job.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will vote for Option C. It is the only one that truly reflects usage. I believe in objective truth.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I will vote for Option B. It gives me the stability I need. I can plan my finances around a fixed seasonal rate.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I will vote for Option B. It feels like a way to keep the peace while still being reasonable.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
